Thanks Adam,
But the endoR function certainly allows you to simulated death from heat stress, when a burrow would be needed, etc. You can also work out how much energy and water would be needed for thermoregulation at a snapshot in the organism's life cycle - a 'static energy budget'. The DEB model allows you to simulate the energy budget in terms of growth, development and reproduction over the whole life cycle of the animal. See bioforecasts.science.unimelb.edu.au/app_direct/deb/ <http://bioforecasts.science.unimelb.edu.au/app_direct/deb/>  We're presently working on integrating it with the endotherm model.
All the best,
Mike

